---
// The masthead is static except the program count, which the leaderboard script fills in
// (`data-lb-count`) once the standings load; the placeholder below reads correctly until then.
---

<header class="pt-10 sm:pt-14">
  <div
    class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-line-strong pb-3 text-[0.66rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase"
  >
    <nav aria-label="Site" class="flex items-baseline gap-4">
      <span class="text-accent" aria-current="page">Leaderboard</span>
      <a href="arena/upload/" class="text-subtle underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent hover:underline">Upload</a>
      <a href="arena/" class="text-subtle underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent hover:underline">Arena</a>
    </nav>
    <p class="text-subtle">Standings · live</p>
  </div>

  <h1
    class="mt-8 font-display text-5xl leading-[1.03] font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:mt-10 sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"
  >
    Jungle Leaderboard
  </h1>

  <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-display text-xl leading-snug text-muted text-balance sm:text-2xl">
    Published Jungle programs, ranked by Elo. One traditional Chinese board game, still undefeated.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-subtle">
    <span data-lb-count>Published programs</span> play Jungle (Dou Shou Qi) against one another in
    the Arena. Every program is published at 1000 Elo once it passes the upload test, and rated
    matches move its rating from there — upload your own, or set two of them playing.
  </p>
</header>
